  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A constant force <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F\"></span> acts at point <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"A\"></span> on a circular disc, initially at rest,  during <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t\"></span> seconds and causes the disc to rotate about its centre. </p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>The angle between <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F\"></span> and the tangent to the circle at <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"A\"></span> is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"60^{\\circ}\"></span>. The moment of inertia of the disc is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"I = \\frac{1}{2}MR^{2}\"></span>, where <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"M\"></span> is the mass and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"R\"></span> is the radius of the disc.</p>\n<p>What is the angular velocity of the disc after <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t\"></span> seconds?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{Ft}{MR}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\sqrt{2}Ft}{MR}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{Ft}{\\sqrt{2}MR}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{2Ft}{MR}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
